{"name":"Tinker Light","hex":"#fbedb8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tinker","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An itinerant tinsmith and mender of household utensils made of metal.","A member of the Irish Traveller community or of other itinerant groups; a gypsy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To work as a tinker.","To fiddle with something in an attempt to fix, mend or improve it, especially in an experimental or unskilled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tinker"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tinker","blocks":[{"text":"Tinker or tinkerer is an archaic term for an itinerant tinsmith who mends household utensils."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tinker_by_Krieger.jpg/330px-Tinker_by_Krieger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinker"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=ap